Marker only - see CONTRIBUTING.md. build() is hand-written: 32-bit glibc
needs GCC (not clang, same reason as the 64-bit glibc recipe) with -m32,
--host=i686-pc-linux-gnu to select the i386 sysdeps tree, and
--disable-werror (clang's own restriction doesn't apply here, but glibc's
-Werror default still trips on some sysdeps code under -m32 the same way
it does on native builds).
gen-ports.py must never regenerate over this.

arch was "i686", which is wrong: scraps filters/resolves packages by the
HOST architecture (SCRAPS_ARCH=x86_64 on every real install), not by the
architecture of the code inside them - every other multilib package here
correctly says arch="x86_64" despite also shipping 32-bit i686 code. With
arch="i686" this package was completely invisible to `scraps add glibc-32`
on a real x86_64 system - the one package the whole multilib chain
(openrc-32, mesa-32, busybox-32, ...) depends on could never actually be
installed. release=2 re-tags the same already-built binary (repackaged,
not rebuilt - this host has no GCC to reproduce glibc-32's build with).
